  "response": "To count embedding and LLM tokens in the current LlamaIndex, you should use the `TokenCountingHandler` callback. This callback is part of the observability features provided by LlamaIndex and is designed to predict token usage for both LLM and embedding calls. Here’s how you can set it up:\n\n1. **Setup `MockLLM` and `MockEmbedding` objects** (if you're doing testing or want to mock these functionalities):\n\n   ```python\n   from llama_index.core.llms import MockLLM\n   from llama_index.core import MockEmbedding\n\n   llm = MockLLM(max_tokens=256)\n   embed_model = MockEmbedding(embed_dim=1536)\n   ```\n\n2. **Setup the `TokenCountingHandler` callback**:\n\n   ```python\n   import tiktoken\n   from llama_index.core.callbacks import CallbackManager, TokenCountingHandler\n\n   token_counter = TokenCountingHandler(\n       tokenizer=tiktoken.encoding_for_model(\"gpt-3.5-turbo\").encode\n   )\n\n   callback_manager = CallbackManager([token_counter])\n   ```\n\n3. **Add them to the global `Settings`**:\n\n   ```python\n   from llama_index.core import Settings\n\n   Settings.llm = llm\n   Settings.embed_model = embed_model\n   Settings.callback_manager = callback_manager\n   ```\n\nThis setup ensures that you can track token usage effectively using the `TokenCountingHandler` callback, which has replaced the previous method of directly tracking token usage on `llm_predictor` and `embed_model` objects. For more details on this migration, you can refer to the \"Token Counting - Migration Guide\" in the documentation.\n\nRelevant documentation references:\n- \"Usage Pattern\" mentions the use of `TokenCountingHandler` for token counting. [\"Usage Pattern\" [1] llama_index/docs/src/content/docs/framework/understanding/evaluating/cost_analysis/usage_pattern.md (lines 1-97)]\n- \"Token Counting - Migration Guide\" explains the transition to using the `TokenCountingHandler` callback. [\"Token Counting - Migration Guide\" [3] llama_index/docs/src/content/docs/framework/module_guides/observability/callbacks/token_counting_migration.md (lines 1-59)]",
